content.thinking:
I found the answer! Looking at the `agents-observe` marketplace.json:

```json
{
  "name": "agents-observe",
  "owner": {
    "name": "simple10"
  },
  "plugins": [
    {
      "name": "agents-observe",
      "description": "Real-time observability dashboard for Claude Code agents",
      "source": "./"
    }
  ]
}
```

The `source` is just a **string** — a path string `"./"` — not an object with `type` and `path` fields!


So I need to update our marketplace.json to use `"source": "./"` instead of the object format. Let me check the official Claude plugins marketplace to see if there are other variations I should be aware of.

